hnswlib — header-only HNSW approximate-nearest-neighbor library
================================================================

Upstream:   https://github.com/nmslib/hnswlib (Apache License 2.0, see LICENSE)
Imported:   from the Percona vector-search prototype (PS-10258, branch
            vector-proto in percona-server-private), which is itself a fork
            of upstream hnswlib.

Percona modifications relative to upstream hnswlib
--------------------------------------------------

1. hnswalg.h: persistence callbacks for HierarchicalNSW:
     - setAddPointInsertCallback(): fired once per addPoint() with the new
       node's label, level and per-level neighbor lists, so the embedding
       storage engine can persist the node.
     - setAddPointUpdateCallback(): fired (batched via
       flushAddPointUpdateCallbackForNeighborIds) for every EXISTING node
       whose neighbor lists were mutated by an addPoint(), so the engine
       can re-persist those nodes.
2. hnswalg.h: loadIndex(const std::vector<VecAuxLoadedRowTuple>&) — rebuild
   the in-memory graph from rows loaded from the InnoDB vector-index
   auxiliary table (label, level, vector, neighbors-by-level), instead of
   from upstream's file-based serialization.
3. hnswlib.h: HNSWERR override hook (upstream PR #508).
4. hnswlib.h: include <x86intrin.h>/<intrin.h> for the USE_SSE-only case —
   the fork's cpuid/xgetbv restructure had left the intrinsics header
   AVX-conditional, breaking SSE-only compilation units.

Used by the InnoDB vector index implementation (PS-11299 storage skeleton,
PS-11300 population). InnoDB is the only in-tree consumer; the library is
header-only and compiled into the innobase target — no separate build.

Local policy: keep diffs against upstream minimal; fixes belong upstream
or in the callback layer, not scattered through the algorithm code.

5. loadIndex(VecAuxLoadedRowTuple): neighbor labels absent from
   label_lookup_ are skipped instead of asserted. A committed row may
   reference a label whose inserting transaction rolled back later
   (cross-transaction link); the aux row for that label is gone, so
   the edge is dropped at load (PS-11300 rollback support).
